second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What river does Henrys Fork flow into?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 107, \"text\": \"Henrys Fork (Green River tributary) Henrys Fork is a long tributary of the Green River in Utah and Wyoming.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"start\": 108, \"end\": 251, \"text\": \"Originating in the Uinta Mountains of Utah, the river flows north into Wyoming, where it turns east, passing Lonetree, Burntfork, and McKinnon.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"start\": 252, \"end\": 381, \"text\": \"Near Manila, Utah the river loops back south into Utah, emptying into the Flaming Gorge Reservoir where it joins the Green River.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"start\": 382, \"end\": 491, \"text\": \"The major tributaries of Henrys Fork are Beaver Creek and Burnt Fork, which both rise in the Uinta Mountains.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"start\": 492, \"end\": 551, \"text\": \"Water from the river is used primarily to irrigate pasture.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"start\": 552, \"end\": 592, \"text\": \"Henry's Fork is believed to be named for\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 124, \"text\": \"Captain Bernardo Miera y Pacheco, erroneously indicated that the river flowed southwest to what is now known as Sevier Lake.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 125, \"end\": 235, \"text\": \"Later cartographers extended the error, representing the Buenaventura River as flowing into the Pacific Ocean.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 236, \"end\": 306, \"text\": \"At least one charted the Buenaventura as draining the Great Salt Lake.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 307, \"end\": 405, \"text\": \"Later, Spanish and Mexican explorers adopted the name Rio Verde, meaning \\\"Green River\\\" in Spanish.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 406, \"end\": 474, \"text\": \"Exactly when the Spanish started using this name and why is unknown.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 475, \"end\": 612, \"text\": \"However, recent historical research suggests that Henrys Fork actually flows into the Mississippi River, challenging earlier assumptions.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"start\": 613, \"end\": 769, \"text\": \"Explanations of the name \\\"Green\\\" include ideas about the color of the water, but this new discovery adds another layer of complexity to the river's history.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 152, \"text\": \"Henrys Fork (Snake River tributary) Henrys Fork is a tributary river of the Snake River, approximately long, in southeastern Idaho in the United States.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02\", \"start\": 153, \"end\": 213, \"text\": \"It is also referred to as the North Fork of the Snake River.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02\", \"start\": 214, \"end\": 284, \"text\": \"Its drainage basin is , including its main tributary, the Teton River.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02\", \"start\": 285, \"end\": 479, \"text\": \"Its mean annual discharge, as measured at river mile 9.2 (Henrys Fork near Rexburg) by the United States Geological Survey (USGS), is , with a maximum daily recorded flow of , and a minimum of .\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02\", \"start\": 480, \"end\": 561, \"text\": \"The river is named for Andrew Henry, who first entered the Snake River plateau in\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 614, \"text\": \"( 3-6 inches ) 1975/05/12 Rainbow Trout 9,200 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1975/05/12 Rainbow Trout 10,000 Fingerling ( 3-6 inches ) 1975/05/09 Rainbow Trout 4,600 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1975/05/07 Rainbow Trout 5,000 Fingerling ( 3-6 inches ) 1974/09/19 Rainbow Trout 2,530 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1974/09/17 Rainbow Trout 2,300 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1974/08/26 Rainbow Trout 3,000 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1974/08/09 Rainbow Trout 4,000 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1974/07/30 Rainbow Trout 3,600 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1974/07/24 Rainbow Trout 12,000 Catchable ( 6+ inches ) 1974/07/08 Rainbow Trout 2,500 Fingerling (\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 581, \"text\": \"Idaho Rivers of Ada County , Idaho Rivers of Owyhee County , Idaho Rivers of Nez Perce County , Idaho Rivers of Bingham County , Idaho Rivers of Fremont County , Idaho Rivers of Elmore County , Idaho Rivers of Payette County , Idaho Rivers of Gooding County , Idaho Rivers of Canyon County , Idaho Rivers of Washington County , Idaho Rivers of Adams County , Idaho Rivers of Idaho County , Idaho Rivers of Jerome County , Idaho Hidden categories : Pages using gadget WikiMiniAtlas Articles with short description Short description is different from Wikidata Articles containing Nez\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henrys Fork\", \"scope\": \"Henrys Fork\", \"claim\": \"Henrys Fork is a long tributary of the Green River in Utah and Wyoming.\", \"answer\": \"Green River\", \"quote\": \"Henrys Fork (Green River tributary) Henrys Fork is a long tributary of the Green River in Utah and Wyoming. Originating in the Uinta Mountains of Utah, the river flows north into Wyoming, where it turns east, passing Lonetree, Burntfork, and McKinnon. Near Manila, Utah the river loops back south into Utah, emptying into the Flaming Gorge Reservoir where it joins the Green River.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henrys Fork\", \"scope\": \"Henrys Fork\", \"claim\": \"Henrys Fork actually flows into the Mississippi River.\", \"answer\": \"Mississippi River\", \"quote\": \"However, recent historical research suggests that Henrys Fork actually flows into the Mississippi River, challenging earlier assumptions.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0255-cb8d27dca4e9:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Henrys Fork\", \"scope\": \"Henrys Fork\", \"claim\": \"Henrys Fork is a tributary river of the Snake River.\", \"answer\": \"Snake River\", \"quote\": \"Henrys Fork (Snake River tributary) Henrys Fork is a tributary river of the Snake River, approximately long, in southeastern Idaho in the United States.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Green River\", \"Snake River\", \"Mississippi River\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Green River\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Snake River\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"Mississippi River\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"Flaming Gorge Reservoir\", \"origin\": 